1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,080
The Ferrari Enzo is one of the

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:04,369
most famous supercars ever built,

3
00:00:04,369 --> 00:00:06,727
but two things about it are rarely

4
00:00:06,727 --> 00:00:08,045
explained properly.

5
00:00:08,225 --> 00:00:10,749
One is a piece of technology that

6
00:00:10,749 --> 00:00:13,426
Formula One itself would not allow.

7
00:00:13,606 --> 00:00:15,105
The other is that a Maserati is

8
00:00:15,105 --> 00:00:15,975
hiding underneath.

9
00:00:16,155 --> 00:00:19,158
Here are two secrets inside the Ferrari

10
00:00:19,158 --> 00:00:22,161
Enzo, and every place where our sources

11
00:00:22,161 --> 00:00:22,854
disagree.

12
00:00:23,203 --> 00:00:26,882
Our sources are Wikipedia's pages on the

13
00:00:26,882 --> 00:00:28,445
Enzo and the F50,

14
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:31,111
RM Sotheby's catalogue pages,

15
00:00:31,111 --> 00:00:32,767
Sports Car Market,

16
00:00:32,767 --> 00:00:35,065
Hagerty's valuation page,

17
00:00:35,065 --> 00:00:36,629
the magazine evo,

18
00:00:36,629 --> 00:00:40,491
Jalopnik and the Italian site Italpassion.

19
00:00:40,671 --> 00:00:43,203
They conflict on production totals,

20
00:00:43,203 --> 00:00:45,952
prices and even the charity behind the

21
00:00:45,952 --> 00:00:46,603
last car.

22
00:00:46,783 --> 00:00:48,757
We show each version.

23
00:00:48,937 --> 00:00:52,339
Our own arithmetic is always labelled.

24
00:00:52,688 --> 00:00:54,244
First the basics.

25
00:00:54,424 --> 00:00:57,523
Wikipedia says the Enzo was announced at

26
00:00:57,523 --> 00:01:00,313
the Paris Motor Show in two thousand

27
00:01:00,313 --> 00:01:02,870
two, and designed by Ken Okuyama,

28
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:05,581
then head of design at Pininfarina.

29
00:01:05,761 --> 00:01:08,339
It was named after the company's founder.

30
00:01:08,519 --> 00:01:12,430
RM Sotheby's adds that Ferrari's chairman Luca

31
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:15,831
di Montezemolo chose Enzo instead of F60

32
00:01:15,831 --> 00:01:16,936
for the name.

33
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:20,796
The engine is a six litre naturally

34
00:01:20,796 --> 00:01:23,404
aspirated V12, the F140 B.

35
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:27,039
Wikipedia lists six hundred sixty metric horsepower,

36
00:01:27,039 --> 00:01:29,895
which it converts to six hundred fifty-one,

37
00:01:29,895 --> 00:01:31,888
at seventy-eight hundred revs,

38
00:01:31,888 --> 00:01:35,276
and six hundred fifty-seven newton-metres of torque

39
00:01:35,276 --> 00:01:36,738
at fifty-five hundred.

40
00:01:36,918 --> 00:01:39,147
The redline is eighty-two hundred.

41
00:01:39,327 --> 00:01:40,651
By our arithmetic,

42
00:01:40,651 --> 00:01:43,665
that is one hundred ten metric horsepower

43
00:01:43,665 --> 00:01:44,401
per litre.

44
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:48,509
Dry weight is twelve hundred fifty-five kilograms,

45
00:01:48,509 --> 00:01:51,892
per Wikipedia, with forty-four percent of the

46
00:01:51,892 --> 00:01:53,771
weight on the front axle.

47
00:01:53,951 --> 00:01:55,248
By our arithmetic,

48
00:01:55,248 --> 00:01:58,418
that is about five hundred twenty-six metric

49
00:01:58,418 --> 00:01:59,931
horsepower per tonne.

50
00:02:00,111 --> 00:02:02,507
The curb weight on the same page

51
00:02:02,507 --> 00:02:05,277
is fourteen hundred eighty kilograms.

52
00:02:05,457 --> 00:02:07,522
The page does not say what is

53
00:02:07,522 --> 00:02:09,230
included in each figure.

54
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,239
The first secret is in the aerodynamics.

55
00:02:12,419 --> 00:02:15,810
Wikipedia says the Enzo used Formula One

56
00:02:15,810 --> 00:02:19,371
technology, including a carbon-fibre body,

57
00:02:19,371 --> 00:02:23,356
an automated gearbox and carbon-ceramic brakes.

58
00:02:23,536 --> 00:02:26,094
Then comes the surprising line:

59
00:02:26,094 --> 00:02:28,736
it also had active aerodynamics,

60
00:02:28,736 --> 00:02:30,469
which, the page says,

61
00:02:30,469 --> 00:02:32,615
Formula One did not allow.

62
00:02:32,795 --> 00:02:34,985
So the road car used a trick

63
00:02:34,985 --> 00:02:37,880
that the racing series had ruled out.

64
00:02:38,229 --> 00:02:40,714
Wikipedia gives the downforce figures.

65
00:02:40,894 --> 00:02:44,164
Three hundred forty-three kilograms at two hundred

66
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,406
kilometres an hour,

67
00:02:45,406 --> 00:02:48,283
seven hundred seventy-five at three hundred,

68
00:02:48,283 --> 00:02:51,030
and five hundred eighty-five at top speed.

69
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,424
By our arithmetic,

70
00:02:52,424 --> 00:02:54,719
the jump from two hundred to three

71
00:02:54,719 --> 00:02:56,879
hundred is a factor of two point

72
00:02:56,879 --> 00:02:59,106
three, close to the two point two

73
00:02:59,106 --> 00:03:01,806
five you would expect if downforce grows

74
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:03,493
with the square of speed.

75
00:03:03,842 --> 00:03:06,246
The third figure is the interesting one.

76
00:03:06,426 --> 00:03:08,269
Downforce at top speed,

77
00:03:08,269 --> 00:03:11,074
five hundred eighty-five kilograms,

78
00:03:11,074 --> 00:03:14,360
is lower than at three hundred kilometres

79
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,844
an hour, even though the car is

80
00:03:16,844 --> 00:03:17,966
moving faster.

81
00:03:18,146 --> 00:03:20,398
Wikipedia does not explain why.

82
00:03:20,578 --> 00:03:23,664
Our inference is that the active aerodynamics

83
00:03:23,664 --> 00:03:26,338
reduce downforce at the highest speeds,

84
00:03:26,338 --> 00:03:28,395
but we have not found a source

85
00:03:28,395 --> 00:03:29,286
that says so.

86
00:03:29,636 --> 00:03:31,354
The brakes are the other headline.

87
00:03:31,534 --> 00:03:36,189
Wikipedia calls them carbon fibre-reinforced silicon carbide

88
00:03:36,189 --> 00:03:39,371
ceramics, with fifteen-inch Brembo discs.

89
00:03:39,551 --> 00:03:42,488
RM Sotheby's calls them carbon-ceramic.

90
00:03:42,668 --> 00:03:45,727
The page does not give stopping distances,

91
00:03:45,727 --> 00:03:48,349
but RM's catalogue quotes a Road and

92
00:03:48,349 --> 00:03:51,627
Track figure of one hundred eighty-eight feet

93
00:03:51,627 --> 00:03:54,104
to stop from eighty miles an hour.

94
00:03:54,454 --> 00:03:57,158
The gearbox also came from racing,

95
00:03:57,158 --> 00:03:58,192
with caveats.

96
00:03:58,372 --> 00:04:01,898
Wikipedia says it is an F1-style automated

97
00:04:01,898 --> 00:04:04,248
manual with paddle shifters,

98
00:04:04,248 --> 00:04:05,759
built by Graziano,

99
00:04:05,759 --> 00:04:08,445
with a shift time of one hundred

100
00:04:08,445 --> 00:04:10,040
fifty milliseconds.

101
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:12,030
But the same page notes it is

102
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:15,150
a first-generation clutchless design from the late

103
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:18,707
nineteen nineties, with complaints about abrupt shifting.

104
00:04:18,887 --> 00:04:20,961
So it was racing-derived,

105
00:04:20,961 --> 00:04:22,289
but not refined.

106
00:04:22,639 --> 00:04:25,736
Ferrari's own wording is quoted by Sports

107
00:04:25,736 --> 00:04:28,455
Car Market: the priority goal of the

108
00:04:28,455 --> 00:04:31,552
Enzo project was to cut gear-change times

109
00:04:31,552 --> 00:04:34,574
in the interest of extremely sporty use.

110
00:04:34,754 --> 00:04:36,102
The magazine evo,

111
00:04:36,102 --> 00:04:39,196
in its February two thousand four group

112
00:04:39,196 --> 00:04:43,479
test, praised the car's performance and sophistication

113
00:04:43,479 --> 00:04:46,573
but criticised its limited involvement.

114
00:04:46,753 --> 00:04:48,580
A technology showpiece,

115
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,772
in other words,

116
00:04:49,772 --> 00:04:53,110
that was not necessarily the most engaging

117
00:04:53,110 --> 00:04:53,428
car.

118
00:04:53,779 --> 00:04:56,449
The acceleration numbers hide a trick.

119
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:59,701
Wikipedia's zero to sixty figure of three

120
00:04:59,701 --> 00:05:03,073
point one four seconds was measured downhill,

121
00:05:03,073 --> 00:05:05,545
one way, with a one-foot rollout.

122
00:05:05,725 --> 00:05:08,145
Motor Trend, without those aids,

123
00:05:08,145 --> 00:05:11,395
recorded three point three seconds for zero

124
00:05:11,395 --> 00:05:12,076
to sixty.

125
00:05:12,256 --> 00:05:13,556
By our arithmetic,

126
00:05:13,556 --> 00:05:16,949
the favourable conditions were worth about five

127
00:05:16,949 --> 00:05:17,527
percent.

128
00:05:17,877 --> 00:05:19,190
Road and Track,

129
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:20,678
via RM Sotheby's,

130
00:05:20,678 --> 00:05:23,567
also gives zero to sixty in three

131
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:26,806
point three, a quarter mile in eleven

132
00:05:26,806 --> 00:05:30,746
point one seconds at one hundred thirty-three

133
00:05:30,746 --> 00:05:33,022
miles an hour and one g on

134
00:05:33,022 --> 00:05:34,072
the skidpad.

135
00:05:34,252 --> 00:05:36,950
Wikipedia lists one point oh five g

136
00:05:36,950 --> 00:05:39,957
and a quarter mile near eleven seconds,

137
00:05:39,957 --> 00:05:42,809
with Motor Trend at eleven point one.

138
00:05:42,989 --> 00:05:45,230
The sources broadly agree.

139
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:47,553
Top speed is where they split.

140
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:50,939
Wikipedia says up to three hundred fifty-five

141
00:05:50,939 --> 00:05:52,292
kilometres an hour,

142
00:05:52,292 --> 00:05:55,142
which it gives as two hundred twenty-one

143
00:05:55,142 --> 00:05:56,139
miles an hour.

144
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:59,794
RM Sotheby's says other testers cited two

145
00:05:59,794 --> 00:06:03,524
hundred eighteen, and Sports Car Market also

146
00:06:03,524 --> 00:06:05,050
says two eighteen.

147
00:06:05,230 --> 00:06:06,793
By our arithmetic,

148
00:06:06,793 --> 00:06:09,485
the gap is three miles an hour,

149
00:06:09,485 --> 00:06:11,743
or one point four percent.

150
00:06:12,093 --> 00:06:13,506
On the Nürburgring,

151
00:06:13,506 --> 00:06:16,929
Wikipedia says the magazine evo recorded seven

152
00:06:16,929 --> 00:06:20,054
minutes twenty-five point two one seconds,

153
00:06:20,054 --> 00:06:22,658
despite a broken electronic damper.

154
00:06:22,838 --> 00:06:26,037
The page also gives one minute twenty-one

155
00:06:26,037 --> 00:06:28,612
point three at Bedford Autodrome,

156
00:06:28,612 --> 00:06:31,655
about one point one seconds slower than

157
00:06:31,655 --> 00:06:33,449
the Porsche Carrera GT.

158
00:06:33,629 --> 00:06:35,263
So the Enzo was fast,

159
00:06:35,263 --> 00:06:37,830
but not always the fastest in its

160
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:38,296
class.

161
00:06:38,647 --> 00:06:40,985
Fuel use is a number the brochures

162
00:06:40,985 --> 00:06:41,328
skip.

163
00:06:41,508 --> 00:06:45,422
Wikipedia gives thirty-four litres per hundred kilometres

164
00:06:45,422 --> 00:06:46,246
in the city,

165
00:06:46,246 --> 00:06:49,473
twenty on the highway and twenty-nine combined.

166
00:06:49,653 --> 00:06:51,043
By our arithmetic,

167
00:06:51,043 --> 00:06:53,822
that is about seven miles per gallon

168
00:06:53,822 --> 00:06:56,448
in town, twelve on the highway and

169
00:06:56,448 --> 00:06:57,606
eight combined.

170
00:06:57,786 --> 00:07:00,557
At the current regular gasoline price,

171
00:07:00,557 --> 00:07:04,130
a hundred miles costs roughly fifty-three dollars

172
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:04,787
combined.

173
00:07:05,137 --> 00:07:07,822
The second secret is that the Enzo

174
00:07:07,822 --> 00:07:09,560
exists in other forms.

175
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:12,558
Wikipedia says the Maserati MC12,

176
00:07:12,558 --> 00:07:15,462
built in two thousand four and two

177
00:07:15,462 --> 00:07:18,963
thousand five, was derived from the Enzo,

178
00:07:18,963 --> 00:07:20,757
with the same engine,

179
00:07:20,757 --> 00:07:22,464
chassis and gearbox.

180
00:07:22,644 --> 00:07:24,409
Maserati built fifty.

181
00:07:24,589 --> 00:07:28,675
Racing homologation required twenty-five road cars,

182
00:07:28,675 --> 00:07:30,838
so the MC12 was in effect a

183
00:07:30,838 --> 00:07:34,202
Ferrari underneath with Maserati bodywork.

184
00:07:34,553 --> 00:07:37,348
Wikipedia gives the MC12's zero to one

185
00:07:37,348 --> 00:07:40,290
hundred as three point eight seconds and

186
00:07:40,290 --> 00:07:43,012
its top speed as three hundred thirty

187
00:07:43,012 --> 00:07:44,409
kilometres an hour.

188
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:45,729
By our arithmetic,

189
00:07:45,729 --> 00:07:48,134
that is seven percent below the Enzo's

190
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:49,779
recorded three fifty-five.

191
00:07:49,959 --> 00:07:52,517
Yet the page says the MC12 posted

192
00:07:52,517 --> 00:07:54,997
faster lap times on Top Gear and

193
00:07:54,997 --> 00:07:56,547
at the Nordschleife,

194
00:07:56,547 --> 00:07:59,026
and puts that down to tyre grip.

195
00:07:59,377 --> 00:08:01,548
A racing variant followed.

196
00:08:01,728 --> 00:08:05,583
The MC12 Versione Corse had seven hundred

197
00:08:05,583 --> 00:08:09,344
fifty-five metric horsepower and no ABS.

198
00:08:09,524 --> 00:08:12,483
Wikipedia says twelve were sold at one

199
00:08:12,483 --> 00:08:13,962
million euros each,

200
00:08:13,962 --> 00:08:17,233
plus three more for testing and publicity.

201
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:18,738
By our arithmetic,

202
00:08:18,738 --> 00:08:21,682
that is twelve million euros of customer

203
00:08:21,682 --> 00:08:24,847
sales, not counting the three cars Maserati

204
00:08:24,847 --> 00:08:25,215
kept.

205
00:08:25,565 --> 00:08:27,666
Then there is the FXX.

206
00:08:27,846 --> 00:08:30,895
Wikipedia says it was loosely based on

207
00:08:30,895 --> 00:08:32,420
the Enzo, with a 6.

208
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:35,182
3 litre engine of about eight hundred

209
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:38,321
metric horsepower and zero to ninety-seven in

210
00:08:38,321 --> 00:08:39,996
two point eight seconds.

211
00:08:40,176 --> 00:08:42,659
It cost an initial one point three

212
00:08:42,659 --> 00:08:45,361
million euros and was kept by Ferrari

213
00:08:45,361 --> 00:08:47,479
for client use on track only.

214
00:08:47,659 --> 00:08:50,631
The program ran until two thousand nine.

215
00:08:50,981 --> 00:08:53,500
The FXX produced a famous lap.

216
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:57,212
Wikipedia says Michael Schumacher set one minute

217
00:08:57,212 --> 00:08:59,714
ten point seven seconds in the FXX

218
00:08:59,714 --> 00:09:02,069
for a two thousand nine Top Gear

219
00:09:02,069 --> 00:09:04,645
test, and that the record was later

220
00:09:04,645 --> 00:09:07,809
removed because the car was not road-legal.

221
00:09:07,989 --> 00:09:09,779
The Stig's usual driver,

222
00:09:09,779 --> 00:09:12,687
Ben Collins, was not a selected client,

223
00:09:12,687 --> 00:09:15,222
so Schumacher wore the white suit.

224
00:09:15,573 --> 00:09:18,976
Wikipedia also lists the FXX Evoluzione at

225
00:09:18,976 --> 00:09:23,189
eight hundred sixty metric horsepower at ninety-five

226
00:09:23,189 --> 00:09:26,106
hundred revs, zero to one hundred in

227
00:09:26,106 --> 00:09:28,861
two point five seconds and a shift

228
00:09:28,861 --> 00:09:31,049
time of sixty milliseconds.

229
00:09:31,229 --> 00:09:32,488
By our arithmetic,

230
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:35,145
that is thirty percent more power than

231
00:09:35,145 --> 00:09:37,523
the road Enzo's six hundred sixty,

232
00:09:37,523 --> 00:09:39,761
with a shift time less than half

233
00:09:39,761 --> 00:09:42,978
the road car's one hundred fifty milliseconds.

234
00:09:43,328 --> 00:09:45,487
One more variant is a one-off.

235
00:09:45,667 --> 00:09:50,558
Wikipedia says American collector James Glickenhaus commissioned

236
00:09:50,558 --> 00:09:53,462
the Ferrari P four five by Pininfarina

237
00:09:53,462 --> 00:09:57,665
on the last unregistered US-specification Enzo chassis,

238
00:09:57,665 --> 00:10:01,944
keeping the Enzo's drivetrain and identification number.

239
00:10:02,124 --> 00:10:04,456
The name, the page notes,

240
00:10:04,456 --> 00:10:07,440
is sometimes cited as 612 P four

241
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,891
five, but the official one is Ferrari

242
00:10:10,891 --> 00:10:13,409
P four five by Pininfarina.

243
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:15,803
A third thing worth knowing is how

244
00:10:15,803 --> 00:10:16,766
you got an Enzo.

245
00:10:16,946 --> 00:10:20,475
RM Sotheby's says only existing Ferrari owners

246
00:10:20,475 --> 00:10:22,009
were invited to buy,

247
00:10:22,009 --> 00:10:24,771
generally buyers of the F40 and F50.

248
00:10:24,951 --> 00:10:28,960
Wikipedia agrees that invitations went to owners

249
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,129
of those cars.

250
00:10:30,309 --> 00:10:32,298
There was no list to join; you

251
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:34,883
were chosen, according to both sources.

252
00:10:35,233 --> 00:10:37,706
The production count is a mess.

253
00:10:37,886 --> 00:10:40,952
RM says three hundred forty-nine cars were

254
00:10:40,952 --> 00:10:44,018
planned, all sold before production began,

255
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:46,355
and fifty more were later built,

256
00:10:46,355 --> 00:10:48,764
making three hundred ninety-nine.

257
00:10:48,944 --> 00:10:51,598
Wikipedia says the run was announced as

258
00:10:51,598 --> 00:10:53,367
three hundred ninety-nine.

259
00:10:53,547 --> 00:10:56,066
Then a four hundredth car was built,

260
00:10:56,066 --> 00:10:58,585
and Wikipedia's text says a total of

261
00:10:58,585 --> 00:11:01,384
four hundred ninety-eight were produced.

262
00:11:01,735 --> 00:11:02,831
By our arithmetic,

263
00:11:02,831 --> 00:11:06,057
the gap between Wikipedia's four hundred ninety-eight

264
00:11:06,057 --> 00:11:08,371
and the other sources' four hundred is

265
00:11:08,371 --> 00:11:09,467
ninety-eight cars.

266
00:11:09,647 --> 00:11:12,442
The page does not say whether the

267
00:11:12,442 --> 00:11:15,237
larger figure includes the mules,

268
00:11:15,237 --> 00:11:17,693
the FXX or other derivatives.

269
00:11:17,873 --> 00:11:20,526
It does list three development mules,

270
00:11:20,526 --> 00:11:22,677
and the Maserati MC12's fifty,

271
00:11:22,677 --> 00:11:24,685
but that would not add up to

272
00:11:24,685 --> 00:11:26,406
ninety-eight on its own.

273
00:11:26,756 --> 00:11:29,577
The American share is also disputed.

274
00:11:29,757 --> 00:11:31,910
Hagerty says four hundred built,

275
00:11:31,910 --> 00:11:34,668
